{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DmfDbp9WBVt5twwRZuuqgz","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Implementation Plan: Share Docs V2 (Documentation Export Enhancements)\n     2→\n     3→## Overview\n     4→\n     5→Enhance the existing documentation export feature with five improvements: (1) export specs and implementation plans from `.vista/ralph/` jobs, (2) inline CDN dependencies for true offline support, (3) track export history with metadata, (4) add light/dark theme toggle and table of contents, and (5) export progress.txt and AGENTS.md from feature planning.\n     6→\n     7→## Current State\n     8→\n     9→The V1 export system (commit `10cb21e`) exports Mermaid diagrams and domain requirements as a self-contained HTML file. Key files:\n    10→\n    11→| File | Role |\n    12→|------|------|\n    13→| `vista/server/services/export_service.py` | `ExportService` with `get_exportable_features()` and `generate_export_html()` |\n    14→| `vista/server/routes/export.py` | GET features tree + POST generate HTML |\n    15→| `vista/server/views/export.html` | Standalone Jinja2 template (CDN Tailwind, Mermaid @11, Marked @15) |\n    16→| `vista/server/views/project.html` | Export Docs button + tree checklist modal |\n    17→| `vista/server/services/progress_service.py` | Reads domain-requirements.md, arch manifests, arch files |\n    18→| `vista/tests/test_export_service.py` | 16 tests |\n    19→\n    20→---\n    21→\n    22→## Phase 1: Progress File & Planning Artifacts Export\n    23→\n    24→**Priority: HIGH** — Low effort, high value. Users already have progress.txt and AGENTS.md in features; they just aren't exported.\n    25→\n    26→### 1a. Extend `get_exportable_features()` to report additional content types\n    27→\n    28→**File:** `vista/server/services/export_service.py`\n    29→**Action:** MODIFY `get_exportable_features()`\n    30→\n    31→Add detection for:\n    32→- `progress.txt` — via `ProgressService.read_progress()` (already exists, returns `dict` with `exists` bool and `content` str)\n    33→- `AGENTS.md` — via `ProgressService.read_agents_md()` (already exists, returns `Optional[str]`)\n    34→- `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` — via `ProgressService.read_implementation_plan()` (already exists, returns `Optional[str]`)\n    35→\n    36→Each feature dict gains new boolean fields:\n    37→```python\n    38→{\n    39→    \"name\": \"...\",\n    40→    \"has_requirements\": True,\n    41→    \"has_progress\": True,        # NEW\n    42→    \"has_agents_md\": True,       # NEW\n    43→    \"has_implementation_plan\": True,  # NEW\n    44→    \"diagrams\": [...]\n    45→}\n    46→```\n    47→\n    48→**Inclusion criteria change:** A feature is exportable if it has diagrams OR requirements OR progress OR agents_md OR implementation_plan. Update the `if not diagrams and not has_requirements` guard.\n    49→\n    50→### 1b. Extend `generate_export_html()` to collect new content\n    51→\n    52→**File:** `vista/server/services/export_service.py`\n    53→**Action:** MODIFY `generate_export_html()`\n    54→\n    55→For each selected feature, additionally read:\n    56→- `ProgressService.read_progress()` → extract `.content` string\n    57→- `ProgressService.read_agents_md()`\n    58→- `ProgressService.read_implementation_plan()`\n    59→\n    60→Add to the feature data dict:\n    61→```python\n    62→features_data.append({\n    63→    \"name\": feature_name,\n    64→    \"diagrams\": diagram_data,\n    65→    \"requirements_md\": requirements_md,\n    66→    \"progress_md\": progress_content,            # NEW\n    67→    \"agents_md\": agents_content,                # NEW\n    68→    \"implementation_plan_md\": plan_content,     # NEW\n    69→})\n    70→```\n    71→\n    72→Extend the `export_data` JSON blob:\n    73→```python\n    74→export_data = {\n    75→    \"diagrams\": export_diagrams,\n    76→    \"requirements\": export_requirements,\n    77→    \"progress\": { feature_name: progress_content, ... },           # NEW\n    78→    \"agents\": { feature_name: agents_content, ... },               # NEW\n    79→    \"implementation_plans\": { feature_name: plan_content, ... },   # NEW\n    80→}\n    81→```\n    82→\n    83→### 1c. Update `ExportRequest` model to include content toggles\n    84→\n    85→**File:** `vista/server/routes/export.py`\n    86→**Action:** MODIFY `ExportFeatureSelection`\n    87→\n    88→Add optional flags for what content types to include:\n    89→```python\n    90→class ExportFeatureSelection(BaseModel):\n    91→    name: str\n    92→    diagrams: list[str]\n    93→    include_requirements: bool = True\n    94→    include_progress: bool = True\n    95→    include_agents: bool = True\n    96→    include_implementation_plan: bool = True\n    97→```\n    98→\n    99→The `generate_export_html()` method reads these flags and skips content types accordingly. This keeps backward compatibility (all default to `True`).\n   100→\n   101→### 1d. Extend export.html template\n   102→\n   103→**File:** `vista/server/views/export.html`\n   104→**Action:** MODIFY\n   105→\n   106→After the domain requirements section for each feature, add collapsible sections for:\n   107→1. **Implementation Plan** — rendered via `marked.parse()`, same styling as requirements\n   108→2. **Progress Log** — rendered as `<pre>` formatted text (progress.txt is not markdown)\n   109→3. **AGENTS.md** — rendered via `marked.parse()`\n   110→\n   111→Each section uses the same card pattern as requirements:\n   112→```html\n   113→{% if feature.implementation_plan_md %}\n   114→<div class=\"bg-gray-800 rounded-lg border border-gray-700 p-6 mt-4\">\n   115→    <h3 class=\"text-lg font-semibold mb-4\">Implementation Plan</h3>\n   116→    <div class=\"requirements-content\" id=\"plan-{{ feature.name }}\"></div>\n   117→</div>\n   118→{% endif %}\n   119→```\n   120→\n   121→Add corresponding JS rendering in `renderAllRequirements()` → rename to `renderAllMarkdown()`:\n   122→```javascript\n   123→function renderAllMarkdown() {\n   124→    // Requirements\n   125→    for (const [name, md] of Object.entries(EXPORT_DATA.requirements)) { ... }\n   126→    // Implementation plans\n   127→    for (const [name, md] of Object.entries(EXPORT_DATA.implementation_plans)) { ... }\n   128→    // Agents\n   129→    for (const [name, md] of Object.entries(EXPORT_DATA.agents)) { ... }\n   130→    // Progress (plain text, not markdown)\n   131→    for (const [name, text] of Object.entries(EXPORT_DATA.progress)) {\n   132→        const el = document.getElementById(`progress-${name}`);\n   133→        if (el) el.textContent = text;  // Use textContent for plain text\n   134→    }\n   135→}\n   136→```\n   137→\n   138→### 1e. Update export modal tree to show new content types\n   139→\n   140→**File:** `vista/server/views/project.html`\n   141→**Action:** MODIFY `renderExportTree()` function\n   142→\n   143→Add indicator badges for new content types:\n   144→```javascript\n   145→${feature.has_progress ? '<span class=\"text-xs text-yellow-600\">+ progress</span>' : ''}\n   146→${feature.has_agents_md ? '<span class=\"text-xs text-purple-600\">+ agents</span>' : ''}\n   147→${feature.has_implementation_plan ? '<span class=\"text-xs text-blue-600\">+ plan</span>' : ''}\n   148→```\n   149→\n   150→Optionally add per-content-type checkboxes within the expanded feature section (below diagram checkboxes), defaulting to checked.\n   151→\n   152→### 1f. Tests\n   153→\n   154→**File:** `vista/tests/test_export_service.py`\n   155→**Action:** MODIFY — add tests\n   156→\n   157→| # | Test | Description |\n   158→|---|------|-------------|\n   159→| 1 | `test_exportable_features_includes_progress_only` | Feature with only progress.txt is exportable |\n   160→| 2 | `test_exportable_features_includes_plan_only` | Feature with only IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md is exportable |\n   161→| 3 | `test_exportable_features_reports_new_flags` | All new boolean flags correctly set |\n   162→| 4 | `test_generate_html_includes_progress` | HTML contains progress content in export_data |\n   163→| 5 | `test_generate_html_includes_plan` | HTML contains implementation plan in export_data |\n   164→| 6 | `test_generate_html_includes_agents` | HTML contains agents content in export_data |\n   165→\n   166→---\n   167→\n   168→## Phase 2: Specs and Implementation Plans from Ralph Jobs\n   169→\n   170→**Priority: HIGH** — The most requested enhancement. Ralph jobs produce specs, plans, and progress that users want to share.\n   171→\n   172→### 2a. Add Ralph artifact scanning to ExportService\n   173→\n   174→**File:** `vista/server/services/export_service.py`\n   175→**Action:** MODIFY — add new static method\n   176→\n   177→```python\n   178→@staticmethod\n   179→def get_exportable_ralph_jobs(project_path: str) -> list[dict]:\n   180→    \"\"\"Return Ralph jobs that have exportable artifacts (plans, specs, progress).\n   181→\n   182→    Scans .vista/ralph/ for job directories containing IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md,\n   183→    specs/*.md, or progress.txt.\n   184→    \"\"\"\n   185→```\n   186→\n   187→Returns:\n   188→```python\n   189→[{\n   190→    \"job_id\": \"uuid\",\n   191→    \"slug\": \"feature-name-plan\",\n   192→    \"mode\": \"plan\",\n   193→    \"status\": \"completed\",\n   194→    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-13T...\",\n   195→    \"has_implementation_plan\": True,\n   196→    \"has_progress\": True,\n   197→    \"has_task\": True,\n   198→    \"spec_files\": [\"spec-one.md\", \"spec-two.md\"],  # from specs/ subdir\n   199→}]\n   200→```\n   201→\n   202→**Implementation approach:**\n   203→- Scan `.vista/ralph/` directories\n   204→- Read `job.json` for metadata (slug, mode, status, created_at)\n   205→- Check for `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, `progress.txt`, `task.md`\n   206→- Scan `specs/` subdirectory for `.md` files (Ralph plan jobs sometimes create specs alongside plans)\n   207→- Group by slug, most recent first\n   208→- **Note:** Ralph jobs store specs in the **feature directory** (`.vista/features/{slug}/specs/`), not in the job dir. The plan co-location logic in `_resolve_plan_dir()` writes plans to the feature dir when it exists. So for most jobs, the exportable plan is actually in the feature directory (already covered by Phase 1). This method focuses on **standalone Ralph jobs** that don't have a corresponding feature directory — their plans live in the job dir.\n   209→\n   210→### 2b. Add Ralph content reading methods\n   211→\n   212→**File:** `vista/server/services/export_service.py`\n   213→**Action:** MODIFY — add helper methods\n   214→\n   215→```python\n   216→@staticmethod\n   217→def read_ralph_artifact(project_path: str, job_slug_dir: str, filename: str) -> Optional[str]:\n   218→    \"\"\"Read a specific file from a Ralph job directory with path traversal prevention.\"\"\"\n   219→```\n   220→\n   221→Uses the same `resolve().relative_to()` pattern as `ProgressService.read_arch_file()`.\n   222→\n   223→### 2c. Extend export API to accept Ralph job selections\n   224→\n   225→**File:** `vista/server/routes/export.py`\n   226→**Action:** MODIFY\n   227→\n   228→Add new request model:\n   229→```python\n   230→class ExportRalphJobSelection(BaseModel):\n   231→    slug_dir: str  # directory name under .vista/ralph/\n   232→    include_plan: bool = True\n   233→    include_progress: bool = True\n   234→    include_task: bool = True\n   235→    include_specs: list[str] = []  # specific spec filenames to include\n   236→\n   237→class ExportRequest(BaseModel):\n   238→    features: list[ExportFeatureSelection]\n   239→    ralph_jobs: list[ExportRalphJobSelection] = []  # NEW, optional\n   240→```\n   241→\n   242→Add new endpoint:\n   243→```python\n   244→@router.get(\"/api/projects/{project_id}/export/ralph-jobs\")\n   245→async def get_export_ralph_jobs(project_id: str):\n   246→    \"\"\"Return Ralph jobs with exportable artifacts for the export modal.\"\"\"\n   247→```\n   248→\n   249→### 2d. Extend `generate_export_html()` for Ralph data\n   250→\n   251→**File:** `vista/server/services/export_service.py`\n   252→**Action:** MODIFY\n   253→\n   254→Accept optional `selected_ralph_jobs` parameter. For each selected job:\n   255→1. Read `task.md` (if selected)\n   256→2. Read `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (if selected)\n   257→3. Read `progress.txt` (if selected)\n   258→4. Read selected spec files from the job directory\n   259→\n   260→Add Ralph jobs as a separate section in the export data:\n   261→```python\n   262→export_data = {\n   263→    \"diagrams\": export_diagrams,\n   264→    \"requirements\": export_requirements,\n   265→    \"progress\": ...,\n   266→    \"agents\": ...,\n   267→    \"implementation_plans\": ...,\n   268→    \"ralph_jobs\": [{          # NEW\n   269→        \"slug\": \"share-docs-plan\",\n   270→        \"mode\": \"plan\",\n   271→        \"status\": \"completed\",\n   272→        \"task_md\": \"...\",\n   273→        \"plan_md\": \"...\",\n   274→        \"progress_text\": \"...\",\n   275→        \"specs\": {\"spec-name.md\": \"...\"},\n   276→    }],\n   277→}\n   278→```\n   279→\n   280→### 2e. Add Ralph section to export.html template\n   281→\n   282→**File:** `vista/server/views/export.html`\n   283→**Action:** MODIFY\n   284→\n   285→After the features sections, add a \"Ralph Development Loops\" section:\n   286→```html\n   287→{% if ralph_jobs %}\n   288→<section class=\"mb-12\">\n   289→    <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\">Development Loops</h2>\n   290→    {% for job in ralph_jobs %}\n   291→    <div class=\"bg-gray-800 rounded-lg border border-gray-700 p-6 mb-4\">\n   292→        <div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mb-4\">\n   293→            <h3 class=\"text-lg font-semibold\">{{ job.slug }}</h3>\n   294→            <span class=\"badge {{ 'badge-arch' if job.mode == 'plan' else 'badge-tdd' }}\">{{ job.mode }}</span>\n   295→            <span class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">{{ job.status }}</span>\n   296→        </div>\n   297→        <!-- Task description, plan, progress rendered via marked/pre -->\n   298→    </div>\n   299→    {% endfor %}\n   300→</section>\n   301→{% endif %}\n   302→```\n   303→\n   304→### 2f. Add Ralph jobs to export modal tree\n   305→\n   306→**File:** `vista/server/views/project.html`\n   307→**Action:** MODIFY\n   308→\n   309→Below the feature checklist, add a \"Development Loops\" section:\n   310→- Fetch from `GET /api/projects/{id}/export/ralph-jobs`\n   311→- Render job entries with checkboxes for plan/progress/task\n   312→- Include in `collectSelectedFeatures()` → rename to `collectExportSelection()`\n   313→\n   314→### 2g. Tests\n   315→\n   316→**File:** `vista/tests/test_export_service.py`\n   317→**Action:** MODIFY\n   318→\n   319→| # | Test | Description |\n   320→|---|------|-------------|\n   321→| 1 | `test_get_exportable_ralph_jobs_finds_jobs` | Jobs with plans are discovered |\n   322→| 2 | `test_get_exportable_ralph_jobs_excludes_empty` | Jobs with only job.json are excluded |\n   323→| 3 | `test_read_ralph_artifact_path_traversal` | Path traversal is blocked |\n   324→| 4 | `test_generate_html_with_ralph_jobs` | HTML includes Ralph job sections |\n   325→| 5 | `test_export_ralph_jobs_endpoint` | GET endpoint returns correct shape |\n   326→\n   327→---\n   328→\n   329→## Phase 3: Offline-First (Inline CDN Dependencies)\n   330→\n   331→**Priority: MEDIUM** — Important for sharing exported files where recipients may not have internet.\n   332→\n   333→### 3a. Download and vendor CDN dependencies\n   334→\n   335→**New directory:** `vista/server/views/static/vendor/`\n   336→\n   337→Download minified versions:\n   338→- `tailwind.min.css` — Use Tailwind standalone CLI to generate a CSS file with only the classes used in `export.html`. This replaces the CDN JIT compiler with a pre-built CSS file (~30-50KB gzipped).\n   339→- `mermaid.min.js` — Download from jsdelivr CDN (~1.5MB minified). This is the largest dependency.\n   340→- `marked.min.js` — Download from jsdelivr CDN (~40KB minified).\n   341→\n   342→**Alternative approach (recommended):** Instead of vendoring files to disk, **fetch and inline at export time**:\n   343→\n   344→### 3b. Add an `InlineDependencyService`\n   345→\n   346→**File:** `vista/server/services/inline_deps_service.py` (NEW)\n   347→\n   348→```python\n   349→class InlineDependencyService:\n   350→    \"\"\"Manages offline-ready dependency bundling for HTML exports.\"\"\"\n   351→\n   352→    VENDOR_DIR = config.STATIC_DIR / \"vendor\"\n   353→\n   354→    # Pre-downloaded minified files\n   355→    DEPS = {\n   356→        \"tailwind_css\": VENDOR_DIR / \"tailwind-export.min.css\",\n   357→        \"mermaid_js\": VENDOR_DIR / \"mermaid.min.js\",\n   358→        \"marked_js\": VENDOR_DIR / \"marked.min.js\",\n   359→    }\n   360→\n   361→    @classmethod\n   362→    def get_inline_deps(cls) -> dict[str, str]:\n   363→        \"\"\"Return dependency contents for inlining into export HTML.\n   364→\n   365→        Returns dict with keys: tailwind_css, mermaid_js, marked_js.\n   366→        Each value is the file content as a string.\n   367→        Falls back to CDN URLs if vendor files are missing.\n   368→        \"\"\"\n   369→```\n   370→\n   371→**Tailwind approach:** Use Tailwind's Play CDN for dev/preview but generate a static CSS file for exports:\n   372→1. Extract all Tailwind utility classes used in `export.html` (they're static — the template uses a fixed set)\n   373→2. Pre-generate a Tailwind CSS file containing only those classes\n   374→3. Store as `vendor/tailwind-export.min.css` (~15-25KB for the specific classes used)\n   375→4. Alternative: Use a pre-compiled Tailwind CSS build that includes all used classes\n   376→\n   377→### 3c. Add offline mode toggle to export API\n   378→\n   379→**File:** `vista/server/routes/export.py`\n   380→**Action:** MODIFY `ExportRequest`\n   381→\n   382→```python\n   383→class ExportRequest(BaseModel):\n   384→    features: list[ExportFeatureSelection]\n   385→    ralph_jobs: list[ExportRalphJobSelection] = []\n   386→    offline: bool = False  # NEW: when True, inline all dependencies\n   387→```\n   388→\n   389→### 3d. Modify template to support both CDN and inline modes\n   390→\n   391→**File:** `vista/server/views/export.html`\n   392→**Action:** MODIFY\n   393→\n   394→Use Jinja2 conditionals:\n   395→```html\n   396→{% if inline_deps %}\n   397→    <style>{{ inline_deps.tailwind_css }}</style>\n   398→    <script>{{ inline_deps.mermaid_js }}</script>\n   399→    <script>{{ inline_deps.marked_js }}</script>\n   400→{% else %}\n   401→    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n   402→    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@11/dist/mermaid.min.js\"></script>\n   403→    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/marked@15/marked.min.js\"></script>\n   404→{% endif %}\n   405→```\n   406→\n   407→**Important:** When inlining, Tailwind CDN script must be replaced with a pre-compiled `<style>` tag since the JIT compiler won't work inline. The `tailwind_css` content must be a CSS file, not the Tailwind JS.\n   408→\n   409→### 3e. Update `generate_export_html()` to pass inline deps\n   410→\n   411→**File:** `vista/server/services/export_service.py`\n   412→**Action:** MODIFY\n   413→\n   414→```python\n   415→def generate_export_html(\n   416→    ...,\n   417→    offline: bool = False,  # NEW\n   418→) -> str:\n   419→    inline_deps = None\n   420→    if offline:\n   421→        inline_deps = InlineDependencyService.get_inline_deps()\n   422→\n   423→    return template.render(\n   424→        ...,\n   425→        inline_deps=inline_deps,\n   426→    )\n   427→```\n   428→\n   429→### 3f. Add offline toggle to export modal\n   430→\n   431→**File:** `vista/server/views/project.html`\n   432→**Action:** MODIFY\n   433→\n   434→Add a checkbox in the modal footer:\n   435→```html\n   436→<label class=\"flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer\">\n   437→    <input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"export-offline\" class=\"rounded\">\n   438→    <span class=\"text-xs text-gray-400\">Offline mode (larger file, no CDN needed)</span>\n   439→</label>\n   440→```\n   441→\n   442→Include in `startExport()`:\n   443→```javascript\n   444→body: JSON.stringify({\n   445→    features: selected,\n   446→    offline: document.getElementById('export-offline').checked,\n   447→}),\n   448→```\n   449→\n   450→### 3g. Generate vendor files (one-time setup task)\n   451→\n   452→**Action:** Create a script or document the process for downloading/generating vendor files.\n   453→\n   454→For Tailwind CSS specifically:\n   455→- Option A: Use `npx tailwindcss` CLI to scan `export.html` and generate minimal CSS\n   456→- Option B: Use a pre-built Tailwind CSS with all utility classes (~300KB)\n   457→- Option C: Replace Tailwind utilities in export.html with hand-written CSS (~5KB) — most reliable but most work\n   458→\n   459→**Recommendation:** Option A is best. Create `vista/server/views/static/vendor/build-tailwind.sh`:\n   460→```bash\n   461→#!/bin/bash\n   462→npx tailwindcss -i ./input.css -o ./tailwind-export.min.css --minify --content ../export.html\n   463→```\n   464→\n   465→### 3h. Tests\n   466→\n   467→**File:** `vista/tests/test_export_service.py`\n   468→**Action:** MODIFY\n   469→\n   470→| # | Test | Description |\n   471→|---|------|-------------|\n   472→| 1 | `test_inline_deps_returns_content_when_vendor_exists` | Service returns file contents |\n   473→| 2 | `test_inline_deps_falls_back_when_missing` | Returns None/empty when vendor files missing |\n   474→| 3 | `test_generate_html_offline_mode` | HTML contains inlined `<style>` and `<script>` tags, no CDN URLs |\n   475→| 4 | `test_generate_html_online_mode` | HTML contains CDN URLs, no inline blocks |\n   476→\n   477→---\n   478→\n   479→## Phase 4: Template Customization (Theme Toggle + Table of Contents)\n   480→\n   481→**Priority: MEDIUM** — Improves usability for printed/shared docs.\n   482→\n   483→### 4a. Add light theme CSS variables\n   484→\n   485→**File:** `vista/server/views/export.html`\n   486→**Action:** MODIFY\n   487→\n   488→Add a CSS custom property system for theming:\n   489→```css\n   490→:root {\n   491→    --bg-primary: #0f172a;\n   492→    --bg-secondary: #1e293b;\n   493→    --bg-card: #1e293b;\n   494→    --border-color: #334155;\n   495→    --text-primary: #e2e8f0;\n   496→    --text-secondary: #cbd5e1;\n   497→    --text-muted: #94a3b8;\n   498→}\n   499→\n   500→:root.light {\n   501→    --bg-primary: #ffffff;\n   502→    --bg-secondary: #f8fafc;\n   503→    --bg-card: #ffffff;\n   504→    --border-color: #e2e8f0;\n   505→    --text-primary: #1e293b;\n   506→    --text-secondary: #475569;\n   507→    --text-muted: #64748b;\n   508→}\n   509→```\n   510→\n   511→Replace all hardcoded color values in the CSS with `var(--...)` references.\n   512→\n   513→### 4b. Add theme toggle button\n   514→\n   515→**File:** `vista/server/views/export.html`\n   516→**Action:** MODIFY\n   517→\n   518→Add a toggle in the header:\n   519→```html\n   520→<button onclick=\"toggleTheme()\" id=\"theme-toggle\" class=\"text-sm px-3 py-1 rounded border\" title=\"Toggle theme\">\n   521→    <span id=\"theme-icon\">☀</span>\n   522→</button>\n   523→```\n   524→\n   525→JavaScript:\n   526→```javascript\n   527→function toggleTheme() {\n   528→    const root = document.documentElement;\n   529→    const isLight = root.classList.toggle('light');\n   530→    document.getElementById('theme-icon').textContent = isLight ? '🌙' : '☀';\n   531→    // Re-render Mermaid diagrams with appropriate theme\n   532→    mermaid.initialize({\n   533→        ...mermaidConfig,\n   534→        theme: isLight ? 'default' : 'dark',\n   535→        themeVariables: isLight ? LIGHT_THEME_VARS : DARK_THEME_VARS,\n   536→    });\n   537→    renderAllDiagrams();  // Re-render with new theme\n   538→    localStorage.setItem('vista-export-theme', isLight ? 'light' : 'dark');\n   539→}\n   540→```\n   541→\n   542→**Mermaid re-rendering note:** Changing Mermaid theme requires re-initializing and re-rendering all diagrams. This is acceptable since exports typically have <20 diagrams.\n   543→\n   544→### 4c. Add table of contents\n   545→\n   546→**File:** `vista/server/views/export.html`\n   547→**Action:** MODIFY\n   548→\n   549→Add a collapsible TOC sidebar/section after the header:\n   550→```html\n   551→<aside id=\"toc\" class=\"...\">\n   552→    <h3 class=\"font-semibold mb-3\">Contents</h3>\n   553→    <nav class=\"space-y-1\">\n   554→        {% for feature in features %}\n   555→        <div>\n   556→            <a href=\"#feature-{{ feature.name }}\" class=\"text-sm hover:text-blue-400\">\n   557→                {{ feature.name | replace('_', ' ') | title }}\n   558→            </a>\n   559→            <div class=\"ml-3 space-y-0.5\">\n   560→                {% if feature.diagrams %}\n   561→                <a href=\"#feature-{{ feature.name }}-diagrams\" class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">Diagrams ({{ feature.diagrams|length }})</a>\n   562→                {% endif %}\n   563→                {% if feature.requirements_md %}\n   564→                <a href=\"#feature-{{ feature.name }}-requirements\" class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">Requirements</a>\n   565→                {% endif %}\n   566→                {% if feature.implementation_plan_md %}\n   567→                <a href=\"#feature-{{ feature.name }}-plan\" class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">Implementation Plan</a>\n   568→                {% endif %}\n   569→            </div>\n   570→        </div>\n   571→        {% endfor %}\n   572→        {% if ralph_jobs %}\n   573→        <div class=\"pt-2 border-t border-gray-700 mt-2\">\n   574→            <span class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider\">Development Loops</span>\n   575→            {% for job in ralph_jobs %}\n   576→            <a href=\"#ralph-{{ job.slug }}\" class=\"text-sm hover:text-blue-400 block mt-1\">\n   577→                {{ job.slug }}\n   578→            </a>\n   579→            {% endfor %}\n   580→        </div>\n   581→        {% endif %}\n   582→    </nav>\n   583→</aside>\n   584→```\n   585→\n   586→**Layout:** Use a responsive approach — TOC as a left sidebar on wide screens, collapsible panel on narrow screens.\n   587→\n   588→### 4d. Add theme preference to export API\n   589→\n   590→**File:** `vista/server/routes/export.py`\n   591→**Action:** MODIFY `ExportRequest`\n   592→\n   593→```python\n   594→class ExportRequest(BaseModel):\n   595→    features: list[ExportFeatureSelection]\n   596→    ralph_jobs: list[ExportRalphJobSelection] = []\n   597→    offline: bool = False\n   598→    default_theme: str = \"dark\"  # NEW: \"dark\" or \"light\"\n   599→```\n   600→\n   601→Pass to template rendering so the initial theme is set correctly.\n   602→\n   603→### 4e. Tests\n   604→\n   605→| # | Test | Description |\n   606→|---|------|-------------|\n   607→| 1 | `test_export_html_contains_toc` | Multiple features → TOC links present |\n   608→| 2 | `test_export_html_single_feature_no_toc` | Single feature → no TOC (optional) |\n   609→| 3 | `test_export_html_light_theme_default` | `default_theme=\"light\"` → `<html class=\"light\">` |\n   610→| 4 | `test_export_html_has_theme_toggle` | HTML contains theme toggle button |\n   611→\n   612→---\n   613→\n   614→## Phase 5: Export History\n   615→\n   616→**Priority: LOW** — Nice-to-have quality-of-life improvement.\n   617→\n   618→### 5a. Create ExportHistory model\n   619→\n   620→**File:** `vista/server/models/export_history.py` (NEW)\n   621→\n   622→```python\n   623→@dataclass\n   624→class ExportHistoryEntry:\n   625→    id: str = field(default_factory=lambda: str(uuid.uuid4())[:8])\n   626→    project_id: str = \"\"\n   627→    exported_at: str = field(default_factory=lambda: datetime.now().isoformat())\n   628→    filename: str = \"\"\n   629→    feature_count: int = 0\n   630→    feature_names: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n   631→    ralph_job_count: int = 0\n   632→    offline: bool = False\n   633→    file_size_bytes: int = 0\n   634→```\n   635→\n   636→Follow the same `to_dict()` / `from_dict()` pattern as `Project` model.\n   637→\n   638→### 5b. Create ExportHistoryService\n   639→\n   640→**File:** `vista/server/services/export_history_service.py` (NEW)\n   641→\n   642→```python\n   643→class ExportHistoryService:\n   644→    \"\"\"Tracks export history per project.\n   645→\n   646→    Storage: ~/.vista/data/export-history/{project_id}.json\n   647→    Format: JSON array of ExportHistoryEntry dicts, newest first.\n   648→    Max entries: 50 per project (oldest auto-pruned).\n   649→    \"\"\"\n   650→\n   651→    HISTORY_DIR = config.DATA_DIR / \"export-history\"\n   652→    MAX_ENTRIES = 50\n   653→\n   654→    @classmethod\n   655→    def record_export(cls, entry: ExportHistoryEntry) -> None: ...\n   656→\n   657→    @classmethod\n   658→    def get_history(cls, project_id: str) -> list[dict]: ...\n   659→\n   660→    @classmethod\n   661→    def clear_history(cls, project_id: str) -> None: ...\n   662→```\n   663→\n   664→Follow the same JSON file persistence pattern as `ChatSessionService`.\n   665→\n   666→### 5c. Record exports in the export route\n   667→\n   668→**File:** `vista/server/routes/export.py`\n   669→**Action:** MODIFY `export_documentation()`\n   670→\n   671→After generating HTML, record the export:\n   672→```python\n   673→entry = ExportHistoryEntry(\n   674→    project_id=project_id,\n   675→    filename=filename,\n   676→    feature_count=len(body.features),\n   677→    feature_names=[f.name for f in body.features],\n   678→    ralph_job_count=len(body.ralph_jobs),\n   679→    offline=body.offline,\n   680→    file_size_bytes=len(html.encode(\"utf-8\")),\n   681→)\n   682→ExportHistoryService.record_export(entry)\n   683→```\n   684→\n   685→### 5d. Add export history API endpoint\n   686→\n   687→**File:** `vista/server/routes/export.py`\n   688→**Action:** MODIFY\n   689→\n   690→```python\n   691→@router.get(\"/api/projects/{project_id}/export/history\")\n   692→async def get_export_history(project_id: str):\n   693→    \"\"\"Return previous export records for this project.\"\"\"\n   694→    ...\n   695→```\n   696→\n   697→### 5e. Show export history in project page\n   698→\n   699→**File:** `vista/server/views/project.html`\n   700→**Action:** MODIFY\n   701→\n   702→Add a small \"Recent Exports\" section inside the export modal (or on the overview tab):\n   703→```html\n   704→<div class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2\">\n   705→    <span>Last exported: Feb 13, 2026 (3 features, offline)</span>\n   706→</div>\n   707→```\n   708→\n   709→### 5f. Tests\n   710→\n   711→| # | Test | Description |\n   712→|---|------|-------------|\n   713→| 1 | `test_record_export_creates_file` | First export creates history file |\n   714→| 2 | `test_record_export_appends` | Multiple exports accumulate |\n   715→| 3 | `test_history_max_entries_pruned` | >50 entries prunes oldest |\n   716→| 4 | `test_get_history_empty` | No history returns empty list |\n   717→| 5 | `test_export_route_records_history` | POST export creates history entry |\n   718→\n   719→---\n   720→\n   721→## Implementation Order\n   722→\n   723→```\n   724→Phase 1 (Progress/Planning Artifacts) ──→ Phase 2 (Ralph Jobs)\n   725→         │                                        │\n   726→         └────────────── Phase 3 (Offline) ───────┘\n   727→                              │\n   728→                         Phase 4 (Theme/TOC)\n   729→                              │\n   730→                         Phase 5 (History)\n   731→```\n   732→\n   733→**Recommended build order:**\n   734→1. **Phase 1** — Foundation: extends existing data flow, minimal new code\n   735→2. **Phase 2** — Builds on Phase 1's template patterns and data structures\n   736→3. **Phase 3** — Independent but benefits from Phase 1+2 template changes being stable\n   737→4. **Phase 4** — CSS refactor is easier after all content sections exist\n   738→5. **Phase 5** — Pure additive, no dependencies\n   739→\n   740→Phases 1 and 2 can be built together. Phase 3 is independent. Phases 4 and 5 are independent of each other.\n   741→\n   742→---\n   743→\n   744→## File Change Summary\n   745→\n   746→| Action | File | Phase(s) |\n   747→|--------|------|----------|\n   748→| MODIFY | `vista/server/services/export_service.py` | 1, 2, 3 |\n   749→| MODIFY | `vista/server/routes/export.py` | 1, 2, 3, 5 |\n   750→| MODIFY | `vista/server/views/export.html` | 1, 2, 3, 4 |\n   751→| MODIFY | `vista/server/views/project.html` | 1, 2, 3 |\n   752→| MODIFY | `vista/tests/test_export_service.py` | 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 |\n   753→| CREATE | `vista/server/services/inline_deps_service.py` | 3 |\n   754→| CREATE | `vista/server/views/static/vendor/` | 3 |\n   755→| CREATE | `vista/server/models/export_history.py` | 5 |\n   756→| CREATE | `vista/server/services/export_history_service.py` | 5 |\n   757→\n   758→---\n   759→\n   760→## Dependencies\n   761→\n   762→- **No new Python packages** for Phases 1, 2, 4, 5\n   763→- **Phase 3** requires a one-time Tailwind CSS build step (npx/bun) to generate the vendor CSS file\n   764→- **Phase 3** requires downloading mermaid.min.js (~1.5MB) and marked.min.js (~40KB) to `static/vendor/`\n   765→\n   766→## Risks & Mitigations\n   767→\n   768→| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |\n   769→|------|--------|-----------|\n   770→| Mermaid.min.js is ~1.5MB, making offline exports large | Export file size ~2MB+ | Document the tradeoff; offline is opt-in |\n   771→| Tailwind JIT CDN → static CSS may miss some classes | Styling breaks in offline mode | Thorough testing; keep CDN as default |\n   772→| Mermaid theme toggle requires full re-render | Brief flash/delay on theme switch | Show loading state during re-render |\n   773→| Ralph job dirs may have stale/corrupt job.json | Scan errors | Wrap in try/except, skip corrupt jobs |\n   774→| Export history JSON could grow unbounded | Disk space | Cap at 50 entries per project, auto-prune |\n   775→| Phase 2 Ralph job scanning is O(n) across all job dirs | Slow for large projects | Cache results, lazy-load in modal |\n   776→\n   777→## Acceptance Criteria\n   778→\n   779→### Phase 1\n   780→- [ ] Export includes progress.txt content for features that have it\n   781→- [ ] Export includes IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md rendered as markdown\n   782→- [ ] Export includes AGENTS.md rendered as markdown\n   783→- [ ] Export modal shows indicators for new content types\n   784→- [ ] All new tests pass\n   785→- [ ] Backward compatible: existing export requests without new fields still work\n   786→\n   787→### Phase 2\n   788→- [ ] Export modal shows Ralph jobs section with checkboxes\n   789→- [ ] Ralph job plans, tasks, and progress appear in exported HTML\n   790→- [ ] Path traversal prevention works for Ralph artifact reads\n   791→- [ ] Jobs without exportable artifacts are excluded from the tree\n   792→\n   793→### Phase 3\n   794→- [ ] Offline mode checkbox in export modal\n   795→- [ ] Offline export file works without internet (open in browser, disconnect, refresh)\n   796→- [ ] Online mode (default) still uses CDN\n   797→- [ ] Vendor files exist and are kept up-to-date\n   798→\n   799→### Phase 4\n   800→- [ ] Theme toggle button in exported HTML switches between dark and light\n   801→- [ ] Mermaid diagrams re-render with correct theme on toggle\n   802→- [ ] Table of contents lists all features and content sections\n   803→- [ ] TOC links scroll smoothly to target sections\n   804→\n   805→### Phase 5\n   806→- [ ] Each export creates a history entry\n   807→- [ ] History visible in export modal or project overview\n   808→- [ ] History capped at 50 entries per project\n   809→- [ ] History includes feature names, date, file size, offline flag\n   810→\n   811→## Spec Versions\n   812→\n   813→| Spec File | Latest Changelog Date |\n   814→|-----------|----------------------|\n   815→| `.vista/features/share-docs/specs/export-service.md` | Initial (no changelog) |\n   816→| `.vista/features/share-docs/specs/export-template.md` | Initial (no changelog) |\n   817→| `.vista/features/share-docs/specs/export-ui.md` | Initial (no changelog) |\n   818→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9de84d10-e2ff-4976-8ef7-e25fd15568bb","uuid":"212d6f2a-8a56-40b7-910b-32369c5ec69c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\.vista\\ralph\\share-docs-v2-plan-6556ab4b-1235-428b-b9d2-da3c725732ac\\IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","content":"# Implementation Plan: Share Docs V2 (Documentation Export Enhancements)\n\n## Overview\n\nEnhance the existing documentation export feature with five improvements: (1) export specs and implementation plans from `.vista/ralph/` jobs, (2) inline CDN dependencies for true offline support, (3) track export history with metadata, (4) add light/dark theme toggle and table of contents, and (5) export progress.txt and AGENTS.md from feature planning.\n\n## Current State\n\nThe V1 export system (commit `10cb21e`) exports Mermaid diagrams and domain requirements as a self-contained HTML file. Key files:\n\n| File | Role |\n|------|------|\n| `vista/server/services/export_service.py` | `ExportService` with `get_exportable_features()` and `generate_export_html()` |\n| `vista/server/routes/export.py` | GET features tree + POST generate HTML |\n| `vista/server/views/export.html` | Standalone Jinja2 template (CDN Tailwind, Mermaid @11, Marked @15) |\n| `vista/server/views/project.html` | Export Docs button + tree checklist modal |\n| `vista/server/services/progress_service.py` | Reads domain-requirements.md, arch manifests, arch files |\n| `vista/tests/test_export_service.py` | 16 tests |\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Progress File & Planning Artifacts Export\n\n**Priority: HIGH** — Low effort, high value. Users already have progress.txt and AGENTS.md in features; they just aren't exported.\n\n### 1a. Extend `get_exportable_features()` to report additional content types\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/export_service.py`\n**Action:** MODIFY `get_exportable_features()`\n\nAdd detection for:\n- `progress.txt` — via `ProgressService.read_progress()` (already exists, returns `dict` with `exists` bool and `content` str)\n- `AGENTS.md` — via `ProgressService.read_agents_md()` (already exists, returns `Optional[str]`)\n- `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` — via `ProgressService.read_implementation_plan()` (already exists, returns `Optional[str]`)\n\nEach feature dict gains new boolean fields:\n```python\n{\n    \"name\": \"...\",\n    \"has_requirements\": True,\n    \"has_progress\": True,        # NEW\n    \"has_agents_md\": True,       # NEW\n    \"has_implementation_plan\": True,  # NEW\n    \"diagrams\": [...]\n}\n```\n\n**Inclusion criteria change:** A feature is exportable if it has diagrams OR requirements OR progress OR agents_md OR implementation_plan. Update the `if not diagrams and not has_requirements` guard.\n\n### 1b. Extend `generate_export_html()` to collect new content\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/export_service.py`\n**Action:** MODIFY `generate_export_html()`\n\nFor each selected feature, additionally read:\n- `ProgressService.read_progress()` → extract `.content` string\n- `ProgressService.read_agents_md()`\n- `ProgressService.read_implementation_plan()`\n\nAdd to the feature data dict:\n```python\nfeatures_data.append({\n    \"name\": feature_name,\n    \"diagrams\": diagram_data,\n    \"requirements_md\": requirements_md,\n    \"progress_md\": progress_content,            # NEW\n    \"agents_md\": agents_content,                # NEW\n    \"implementation_plan_md\": plan_content,     # NEW\n})\n```\n\nExtend the `export_data` JSON blob:\n```python\nexport_data = {\n    \"diagrams\": export_diagrams,\n    \"requirements\": export_requirements,\n    \"progress\": { feature_name: progress_content, ... },           # NEW\n    \"agents\": { feature_name: agents_content, ... },               # NEW\n    \"implementation_plans\": { feature_name: plan_content, ... },   # NEW\n}\n```\n\n### 1c. Update `ExportRequest` model to include content toggles\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/export.py`\n**Action:** MODIFY `ExportFeatureSelection`\n\nAdd optional flags for what content types to include:\n```python\nclass ExportFeatureSelection(BaseModel):\n    name: str\n    diagrams: list[str]\n    include_requirements: bool = True\n    include_progress: bool = True\n    include_agents: bool = True\n    include_implementation_plan: bool = True\n```\n\nThe `generate_export_html()` method reads these flags and skips content types accordingly. This keeps backward compatibility (all default to `True`).\n\n### 1d. Extend export.html template\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/export.html`\n**Action:** MODIFY\n\nAfter the domain requirements section for each feature, add collapsible sections for:\n1. **Implementation Plan** — rendered via `marked.parse()`, same styling as requirements\n2. **Progress Log** — rendered as `<pre>` formatted text (progress.txt is not markdown)\n3. **AGENTS.md** — rendered via `marked.parse()`\n\nEach section uses the same card pattern as requirements:\n```html\n{% if feature.implementation_plan_md %}\n<div class=\"bg-gray-800 rounded-lg border border-gray-700 p-6 mt-4\">\n    <h3 class=\"text-lg font-semibold mb-4\">Implementation Plan</h3>\n    <div class=\"requirements-content\" id=\"plan-{{ feature.name }}\"></div>\n</div>\n{% endif %}\n```\n\nAdd corresponding JS rendering in `renderAllRequirements()` → rename to `renderAllMarkdown()`:\n```javascript\nfunction renderAllMarkdown() {\n    // Requirements\n    for (const [name, md] of Object.entries(EXPORT_DATA.requirements)) { ... }\n    // Implementation plans\n    for (const [name, md] of Object.entries(EXPORT_DATA.implementation_plans)) { ... }\n    // Agents\n    for (const [name, md] of Object.entries(EXPORT_DATA.agents)) { ... }\n    // Progress (plain text, not markdown)\n    for (const [name, text] of Object.entries(EXPORT_DATA.progress)) {\n        const el = document.getElementById(`progress-${name}`);\n        if (el) el.textContent = text;  // Use textContent for plain text\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 1e. Update export modal tree to show new content types\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/project.html`\n**Action:** MODIFY `renderExportTree()` function\n\nAdd indicator badges for new content types:\n```javascript\n${feature.has_progress ? '<span class=\"text-xs text-yellow-600\">+ progress</span>' : ''}\n${feature.has_agents_md ? '<span class=\"text-xs text-purple-600\">+ agents</span>' : ''}\n${feature.has_implementation_plan ? '<span class=\"text-xs text-blue-600\">+ plan</span>' : ''}\n```\n\nOptionally add per-content-type checkboxes within the expanded feature section (below diagram checkboxes), defaulting to checked.\n\n### 1f. Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_export_service.py`\n**Action:** MODIFY — add tests\n\n| # | Test | Description |\n|---|------|-------------|\n| 1 | `test_exportable_features_includes_progress_only` | Feature with only progress.txt is exportable |\n| 2 | `test_exportable_features_includes_plan_only` | Feature with only IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md is exportable |\n| 3 | `test_exportable_features_reports_new_flags` | All new boolean flags correctly set |\n| 4 | `test_generate_html_includes_progress` | HTML contains progress content in export_data |\n| 5 | `test_generate_html_includes_plan` | HTML contains implementation plan in export_data |\n| 6 | `test_generate_html_includes_agents` | HTML contains agents content in export_data |\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Specs and Implementation Plans from Ralph Jobs\n\n**Priority: HIGH** — The most requested enhancement. Ralph jobs produce specs, plans, and progress that users want to share.\n\n### 2a. Add Ralph artifact scanning to ExportService\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/export_service.py`\n**Action:** MODIFY — add new static method\n\n```python\n@staticmethod\ndef get_exportable_ralph_jobs(project_path: str) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"Return Ralph jobs that have exportable artifacts (plans, specs, progress).\n\n    Scans .vista/ralph/ for job directories containing IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md,\n    specs/*.md, or progress.txt.\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\nReturns:\n```python\n[{\n    \"job_id\": \"uuid\",\n    \"slug\": \"feature-name-plan\",\n    \"mode\": \"plan\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-13T...\",\n    \"has_implementation_plan\": True,\n    \"has_progress\": True,\n    \"has_task\": True,\n    \"spec_files\": [\"spec-one.md\", \"spec-two.md\"],  # from specs/ subdir\n}]\n```\n\n**Implementation approach:**\n- Scan `.vista/ralph/` directories\n- Read `job.json` for metadata (slug, mode, status, created_at)\n- Check for `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, `progress.txt`, `task.md`\n- Scan `specs/` subdirectory for `.md` files (Ralph plan jobs sometimes create specs alongside plans)\n- Group by slug, most recent first\n- **Note:** Ralph jobs store specs in the **feature directory** (`.vista/features/{slug}/specs/`), not in the job dir. The plan co-location logic in `_resolve_plan_dir()` writes plans to the feature dir when it exists. So for most jobs, the exportable plan is actually in the feature directory (already covered by Phase 1). This method focuses on **standalone Ralph jobs** that don't have a corresponding feature directory — their plans live in the job dir.\n\n### 2b. Add Ralph content reading methods\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/export_service.py`\n**Action:** MODIFY — add helper methods\n\n```python\n@staticmethod\ndef read_ralph_artifact(project_path: str, job_slug_dir: str, filename: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"Read a specific file from a Ralph job directory with path traversal prevention.\"\"\"\n```\n\nUses the same `resolve().relative_to()` pattern as `ProgressService.read_arch_file()`.\n\n### 2c. Extend export API to accept Ralph job selections\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/export.py`\n**Action:** MODIFY\n\nAdd new request model:\n```python\nclass ExportRalphJobSelection(BaseModel):\n    slug_dir: str  # directory name under .vista/ralph/\n    include_plan: bool = True\n    include_progress: bool = True\n    include_task: bool = True\n    include_specs: list[str] = []  # specific spec filenames to include\n\nclass ExportRequest(BaseModel):\n    features: list[ExportFeatureSelection]\n    ralph_jobs: list[ExportRalphJobSelection] = []  # NEW, optional\n```\n\nAdd new endpoint:\n```python\n@router.get(\"/api/projects/{project_id}/export/ralph-jobs\")\nasync def get_export_ralph_jobs(project_id: str):\n    \"\"\"Return Ralph jobs with exportable artifacts for the export modal.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### 2d. Extend `generate_export_html()` for Ralph data\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/export_service.py`\n**Action:** MODIFY\n\nAccept optional `selected_ralph_jobs` parameter. For each selected job:\n1. Read `task.md` (if selected)\n2. Read `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (if selected)\n3. Read `progress.txt` (if selected)\n4. Read selected spec files from the job directory\n\nAdd Ralph jobs as a separate section in the export data:\n```python\nexport_data = {\n    \"diagrams\": export_diagrams,\n    \"requirements\": export_requirements,\n    \"progress\": ...,\n    \"agents\": ...,\n    \"implementation_plans\": ...,\n    \"ralph_jobs\": [{          # NEW\n        \"slug\": \"share-docs-plan\",\n        \"mode\": \"plan\",\n        \"status\": \"completed\",\n        \"task_md\": \"...\",\n        \"plan_md\": \"...\",\n        \"progress_text\": \"...\",\n        \"specs\": {\"spec-name.md\": \"...\"},\n    }],\n}\n```\n\n### 2e. Add Ralph section to export.html template\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/export.html`\n**Action:** MODIFY\n\nAfter the features sections, add a \"Ralph Development Loops\" section:\n```html\n{% if ralph_jobs %}\n<section class=\"mb-12\">\n    <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\">Development Loops</h2>\n    {% for job in ralph_jobs %}\n    <div class=\"bg-gray-800 rounded-lg border border-gray-700 p-6 mb-4\">\n        <div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mb-4\">\n            <h3 class=\"text-lg font-semibold\">{{ job.slug }}</h3>\n            <span class=\"badge {{ 'badge-arch' if job.mode == 'plan' else 'badge-tdd' }}\">{{ job.mode }}</span>\n            <span class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">{{ job.status }}</span>\n        </div>\n        <!-- Task description, plan, progress rendered via marked/pre -->\n    </div>\n    {% endfor %}\n</section>\n{% endif %}\n```\n\n### 2f. Add Ralph jobs to export modal tree\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/project.html`\n**Action:** MODIFY\n\nBelow the feature checklist, add a \"Development Loops\" section:\n- Fetch from `GET /api/projects/{id}/export/ralph-jobs`\n- Render job entries with checkboxes for plan/progress/task\n- Include in `collectSelectedFeatures()` → rename to `collectExportSelection()`\n\n### 2g. Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_export_service.py`\n**Action:** MODIFY\n\n| # | Test | Description |\n|---|------|-------------|\n| 1 | `test_get_exportable_ralph_jobs_finds_jobs` | Jobs with plans are discovered |\n| 2 | `test_get_exportable_ralph_jobs_excludes_empty` | Jobs with only job.json are excluded |\n| 3 | `test_read_ralph_artifact_path_traversal` | Path traversal is blocked |\n| 4 | `test_generate_html_with_ralph_jobs` | HTML includes Ralph job sections |\n| 5 | `test_export_ralph_jobs_endpoint` | GET endpoint returns correct shape |\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Offline-First (Inline CDN Dependencies)\n\n**Priority: MEDIUM** — Important for sharing exported files where recipients may not have internet.\n\n### 3a. Download and vendor CDN dependencies\n\n**New directory:** `vista/server/views/static/vendor/`\n\nDownload minified versions:\n- `tailwind.min.css` — Use Tailwind standalone CLI to generate a CSS file with only the classes used in `export.html`. This replaces the CDN JIT compiler with a pre-built CSS file (~30-50KB gzipped).\n- `mermaid.min.js` — Download from jsdelivr CDN (~1.5MB minified). This is the largest dependency.\n- `marked.min.js` — Download from jsdelivr CDN (~40KB minified).\n\n**Alternative approach (recommended):** Instead of vendoring files to disk, **fetch and inline at export time**:\n\n### 3b. Add an `InlineDependencyService`\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/inline_deps_service.py` (NEW)\n\n```python\nclass InlineDependencyService:\n    \"\"\"Manages offline-ready dependency bundling for HTML exports.\"\"\"\n\n    VENDOR_DIR = config.STATIC_DIR / \"vendor\"\n\n    # Pre-downloaded minified files\n    DEPS = {\n        \"tailwind_css\": VENDOR_DIR / \"tailwind-export.min.css\",\n        \"mermaid_js\": VENDOR_DIR / \"mermaid.min.js\",\n        \"marked_js\": VENDOR_DIR / \"marked.min.js\",\n    }\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_inline_deps(cls) -> dict[str, str]:\n        \"\"\"Return dependency contents for inlining into export HTML.\n\n        Returns dict with keys: tailwind_css, mermaid_js, marked_js.\n        Each value is the file content as a string.\n        Falls back to CDN URLs if vendor files are missing.\n        \"\"\"\n```\n\n**Tailwind approach:** Use Tailwind's Play CDN for dev/preview but generate a static CSS file for exports:\n1. Extract all Tailwind utility classes used in `export.html` (they're static — the template uses a fixed set)\n2. Pre-generate a Tailwind CSS file containing only those classes\n3. Store as `vendor/tailwind-export.min.css` (~15-25KB for the specific classes used)\n4. Alternative: Use a pre-compiled Tailwind CSS build that includes all used classes\n\n### 3c. Add offline mode toggle to export API\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/export.py`\n**Action:** MODIFY `ExportRequest`\n\n```python\nclass ExportRequest(BaseModel):\n    features: list[ExportFeatureSelection]\n    ralph_jobs: list[ExportRalphJobSelection] = []\n    offline: bool = False  # NEW: when True, inline all dependencies\n```\n\n### 3d. Modify template to support both CDN and inline modes\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/export.html`\n**Action:** MODIFY\n\nUse Jinja2 conditionals:\n```html\n{% if inline_deps %}\n    <style>{{ inline_deps.tailwind_css }}</style>\n    <script>{{ inline_deps.mermaid_js }}</script>\n    <script>{{ inline_deps.marked_js }}</script>\n{% else %}\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@11/dist/mermaid.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/marked@15/marked.min.js\"></script>\n{% endif %}\n```\n\n**Important:** When inlining, Tailwind CDN script must be replaced with a pre-compiled `<style>` tag since the JIT compiler won't work inline. The `tailwind_css` content must be a CSS file, not the Tailwind JS.\n\n### 3e. Update `generate_export_html()` to pass inline deps\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/export_service.py`\n**Action:** MODIFY\n\n```python\ndef generate_export_html(\n    ...,\n    offline: bool = False,  # NEW\n) -> str:\n    inline_deps = None\n    if offline:\n        inline_deps = InlineDependencyService.get_inline_deps()\n\n    return template.render(\n        ...,\n        inline_deps=inline_deps,\n    )\n```\n\n### 3f. Add offline toggle to export modal\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/project.html`\n**Action:** MODIFY\n\nAdd a checkbox in the modal footer:\n```html\n<label class=\"flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer\">\n    <input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"export-offline\" class=\"rounded\">\n    <span class=\"text-xs text-gray-400\">Offline mode (larger file, no CDN needed)</span>\n</label>\n```\n\nInclude in `startExport()`:\n```javascript\nbody: JSON.stringify({\n    features: selected,\n    offline: document.getElementById('export-offline').checked,\n}),\n```\n\n### 3g. Generate vendor files (one-time setup task)\n\n**Action:** Create a script or document the process for downloading/generating vendor files.\n\nFor Tailwind CSS specifically:\n- Option A: Use `npx tailwindcss` CLI to scan `export.html` and generate minimal CSS\n- Option B: Use a pre-built Tailwind CSS with all utility classes (~300KB)\n- Option C: Replace Tailwind utilities in export.html with hand-written CSS (~5KB) — most reliable but most work\n\n**Recommendation:** Option A is best. Create `vista/server/views/static/vendor/build-tailwind.sh`:\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nnpx tailwindcss -i ./input.css -o ./tailwind-export.min.css --minify --content ../export.html\n```\n\n### 3h. Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_export_service.py`\n**Action:** MODIFY\n\n| # | Test | Description |\n|---|------|-------------|\n| 1 | `test_inline_deps_returns_content_when_vendor_exists` | Service returns file contents |\n| 2 | `test_inline_deps_falls_back_when_missing` | Returns None/empty when vendor files missing |\n| 3 | `test_generate_html_offline_mode` | HTML contains inlined `<style>` and `<script>` tags, no CDN URLs |\n| 4 | `test_generate_html_online_mode` | HTML contains CDN URLs, no inline blocks |\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Template Customization (Theme Toggle + Table of Contents)\n\n**Priority: MEDIUM** — Improves usability for printed/shared docs.\n\n### 4a. Add light theme CSS variables\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/export.html`\n**Action:** MODIFY\n\nAdd a CSS custom property system for theming:\n```css\n:root {\n    --bg-primary: #0f172a;\n    --bg-secondary: #1e293b;\n    --bg-card: #1e293b;\n    --border-color: #334155;\n    --text-primary: #e2e8f0;\n    --text-secondary: #cbd5e1;\n    --text-muted: #94a3b8;\n}\n\n:root.light {\n    --bg-primary: #ffffff;\n    --bg-secondary: #f8fafc;\n    --bg-card: #ffffff;\n    --border-color: #e2e8f0;\n    --text-primary: #1e293b;\n    --text-secondary: #475569;\n    --text-muted: #64748b;\n}\n```\n\nReplace all hardcoded color values in the CSS with `var(--...)` references.\n\n### 4b. Add theme toggle button\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/export.html`\n**Action:** MODIFY\n\nAdd a toggle in the header:\n```html\n<button onclick=\"toggleTheme()\" id=\"theme-toggle\" class=\"text-sm px-3 py-1 rounded border\" title=\"Toggle theme\">\n    <span id=\"theme-icon\">☀</span>\n</button>\n```\n\nJavaScript:\n```javascript\nfunction toggleTheme() {\n    const root = document.documentElement;\n    const isLight = root.classList.toggle('light');\n    document.getElementById('theme-icon').textContent = isLight ? '🌙' : '☀';\n    // Re-render Mermaid diagrams with appropriate theme\n    mermaid.initialize({\n        ...mermaidConfig,\n        theme: isLight ? 'default' : 'dark',\n        themeVariables: isLight ? LIGHT_THEME_VARS : DARK_THEME_VARS,\n    });\n    renderAllDiagrams();  // Re-render with new theme\n    localStorage.setItem('vista-export-theme', isLight ? 'light' : 'dark');\n}\n```\n\n**Mermaid re-rendering note:** Changing Mermaid theme requires re-initializing and re-rendering all diagrams. This is acceptable since exports typically have <20 diagrams.\n\n### 4c. Add table of contents\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/export.html`\n**Action:** MODIFY\n\nAdd a collapsible TOC sidebar/section after the header:\n```html\n<aside id=\"toc\" class=\"...\">\n    <h3 class=\"font-semibold mb-3\">Contents</h3>\n    <nav class=\"space-y-1\">\n        {% for feature in features %}\n        <div>\n            <a href=\"#feature-{{ feature.name }}\" class=\"text-sm hover:text-blue-400\">\n                {{ feature.name | replace('_', ' ') | title }}\n            </a>\n            <div class=\"ml-3 space-y-0.5\">\n                {% if feature.diagrams %}\n                <a href=\"#feature-{{ feature.name }}-diagrams\" class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">Diagrams ({{ feature.diagrams|length }})</a>\n                {% endif %}\n                {% if feature.requirements_md %}\n                <a href=\"#feature-{{ feature.name }}-requirements\" class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">Requirements</a>\n                {% endif %}\n                {% if feature.implementation_plan_md %}\n                <a href=\"#feature-{{ feature.name }}-plan\" class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">Implementation Plan</a>\n                {% endif %}\n            </div>\n        </div>\n        {% endfor %}\n        {% if ralph_jobs %}\n        <div class=\"pt-2 border-t border-gray-700 mt-2\">\n            <span class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider\">Development Loops</span>\n            {% for job in ralph_jobs %}\n            <a href=\"#ralph-{{ job.slug }}\" class=\"text-sm hover:text-blue-400 block mt-1\">\n                {{ job.slug }}\n            </a>\n            {% endfor %}\n        </div>\n        {% endif %}\n    </nav>\n</aside>\n```\n\n**Layout:** Use a responsive approach — TOC as a left sidebar on wide screens, collapsible panel on narrow screens.\n\n### 4d. Add theme preference to export API\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/export.py`\n**Action:** MODIFY `ExportRequest`\n\n```python\nclass ExportRequest(BaseModel):\n    features: list[ExportFeatureSelection]\n    ralph_jobs: list[ExportRalphJobSelection] = []\n    offline: bool = False\n    default_theme: str = \"dark\"  # NEW: \"dark\" or \"light\"\n```\n\nPass to template rendering so the initial theme is set correctly.\n\n### 4e. Tests\n\n| # | Test | Description |\n|---|------|-------------|\n| 1 | `test_export_html_contains_toc` | Multiple features → TOC links present |\n| 2 | `test_export_html_single_feature_no_toc` | Single feature → no TOC (optional) |\n| 3 | `test_export_html_light_theme_default` | `default_theme=\"light\"` → `<html class=\"light\">` |\n| 4 | `test_export_html_has_theme_toggle` | HTML contains theme toggle button |\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Export History\n\n**Priority: LOW** — Nice-to-have quality-of-life improvement.\n\n### 5a. Create ExportHistory model\n\n**File:** `vista/server/models/export_history.py` (NEW)\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass ExportHistoryEntry:\n    id: str = field(default_factory=lambda: str(uuid.uuid4())[:8])\n    project_id: str = \"\"\n    exported_at: str = field(default_factory=lambda: datetime.now().isoformat())\n    filename: str = \"\"\n    feature_count: int = 0\n    feature_names: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n    ralph_job_count: int = 0\n    offline: bool = False\n    file_size_bytes: int = 0\n```\n\nFollow the same `to_dict()` / `from_dict()` pattern as `Project` model.\n\n### 5b. Create ExportHistoryService\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/export_history_service.py` (NEW)\n\n```python\nclass ExportHistoryService:\n    \"\"\"Tracks export history per project.\n\n    Storage: ~/.vista/data/export-history/{project_id}.json\n    Format: JSON array of ExportHistoryEntry dicts, newest first.\n    Max entries: 50 per project (oldest auto-pruned).\n    \"\"\"\n\n    HISTORY_DIR = config.DATA_DIR / \"export-history\"\n    MAX_ENTRIES = 50\n\n    @classmethod\n    def record_export(cls, entry: ExportHistoryEntry) -> None: ...\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_history(cls, project_id: str) -> list[dict]: ...\n\n    @classmethod\n    def clear_history(cls, project_id: str) -> None: ...\n```\n\nFollow the same JSON file persistence pattern as `ChatSessionService`.\n\n### 5c. Record exports in the export route\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/export.py`\n**Action:** MODIFY `export_documentation()`\n\nAfter generating HTML, record the export:\n```python\nentry = ExportHistoryEntry(\n    project_id=project_id,\n    filename=filename,\n    feature_count=len(body.features),\n    feature_names=[f.name for f in body.features],\n    ralph_job_count=len(body.ralph_jobs),\n    offline=body.offline,\n    file_size_bytes=len(html.encode(\"utf-8\")),\n)\nExportHistoryService.record_export(entry)\n```\n\n### 5d. Add export history API endpoint\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/export.py`\n**Action:** MODIFY\n\n```python\n@router.get(\"/api/projects/{project_id}/export/history\")\nasync def get_export_history(project_id: str):\n    \"\"\"Return previous export records for this project.\"\"\"\n    ...\n```\n\n### 5e. Show export history in project page\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/project.html`\n**Action:** MODIFY\n\nAdd a small \"Recent Exports\" section inside the export modal (or on the overview tab):\n```html\n<div class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2\">\n    <span>Last exported: Feb 13, 2026 (3 features, offline)</span>\n</div>\n```\n\n### 5f. Tests\n\n| # | Test | Description |\n|---|------|-------------|\n| 1 | `test_record_export_creates_file` | First export creates history file |\n| 2 | `test_record_export_appends` | Multiple exports accumulate |\n| 3 | `test_history_max_entries_pruned` | >50 entries prunes oldest |\n| 4 | `test_get_history_empty` | No history returns empty list |\n| 5 | `test_export_route_records_history` | POST export creates history entry |\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Progress/Planning Artifacts) ──→ Phase 2 (Ralph Jobs)\n         │                                        │\n         └────────────── Phase 3 (Offline) ───────┘\n                              │\n                         Phase 4 (Theme/TOC)\n                              │\n                         Phase 5 (History)\n```\n\n**Recommended build order:**\n1. **Phase 1** — Foundation: extends existing data flow, minimal new code\n2. **Phase 2** — Builds on Phase 1's template patterns and data structures\n3. **Phase 3** — Independent but benefits from Phase 1+2 template changes being stable\n4. **Phase 4** — CSS refactor is easier after all content sections exist\n5. **Phase 5** — Pure additive, no dependencies\n\nPhases 1 and 2 can be built together. Phase 3 is independent. Phases 4 and 5 are independent of each other.\n\n---\n\n## File Change Summary\n\n| Action | File | Phase(s) |\n|--------|------|----------|\n| MODIFY | `vista/server/services/export_service.py` | 1, 2, 3 |\n| MODIFY | `vista/server/routes/export.py` | 1, 2, 3, 5 |\n| MODIFY | `vista/server/views/export.html` | 1, 2, 3, 4 |\n| MODIFY | `vista/server/views/project.html` | 1, 2, 3 |\n| MODIFY | `vista/tests/test_export_service.py` | 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 |\n| CREATE | `vista/server/services/inline_deps_service.py` | 3 |\n| CREATE | `vista/server/views/static/vendor/` | 3 |\n| CREATE | `vista/server/models/export_history.py` | 5 |\n| CREATE | `vista/server/services/export_history_service.py` | 5 |\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- **No new Python packages** for Phases 1, 2, 4, 5\n- **Phase 3** requires a one-time Tailwind CSS build step (npx/bun) to generate the vendor CSS file\n- **Phase 3** requires downloading mermaid.min.js (~1.5MB) and marked.min.js (~40KB) to `static/vendor/`\n\n## Risks & Mitigations\n\n| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|--------|-----------|\n| Mermaid.min.js is ~1.5MB, making offline exports large | Export file size ~2MB+ | Document the tradeoff; offline is opt-in |\n| Tailwind JIT CDN → static CSS may miss some classes | Styling breaks in offline mode | Thorough testing; keep CDN as default |\n| Mermaid theme toggle requires full re-render | Brief flash/delay on theme switch | Show loading state during re-render |\n| Ralph job dirs may have stale/corrupt job.json | Scan errors | Wrap in try/except, skip corrupt jobs |\n| Export history JSON could grow unbounded | Disk space | Cap at 50 entries per project, auto-prune |\n| Phase 2 Ralph job scanning is O(n) across all job dirs | Slow for large projects | Cache results, lazy-load in modal |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n### Phase 1\n- [ ] Export includes progress.txt content for features that have it\n- [ ] Export includes IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md rendered as markdown\n- [ ] Export includes AGENTS.md rendered as markdown\n- [ ] Export modal shows indicators for new content types\n- [ ] All new tests pass\n- [ ] Backward compatible: existing export requests without new fields still work\n\n### Phase 2\n- [ ] Export modal shows Ralph jobs section with checkboxes\n- [ ] Ralph job plans, tasks, and progress appear in exported HTML\n- [ ] Path traversal prevention works for Ralph artifact reads\n- [ ] Jobs without exportable artifacts are excluded from the tree\n\n### Phase 3\n- [ ] Offline mode checkbox in export modal\n- [ ] Offline export file works without internet (open in browser, disconnect, refresh)\n- [ ] Online mode (default) still uses CDN\n- [ ] Vendor files exist and are kept up-to-date\n\n### Phase 4\n- [ ] Theme toggle button in exported HTML switches between dark and light\n- [ ] Mermaid diagrams re-render with correct theme on toggle\n- [ ] Table of contents lists all features and content sections\n- [ ] TOC links scroll smoothly to target sections\n\n### Phase 5\n- [ ] Each export creates a history entry\n- [ ] History visible in export modal or project overview\n- [ ] History capped at 50 entries per project\n- [ ] History includes feature names, date, file size, offline flag\n\n## Spec Versions\n\n| Spec File | Latest Changelog Date |\n|-----------|----------------------|\n| `.vista/features/share-docs/specs/export-service.md` | Initial (no changelog) |\n| `.vista/features/share-docs/specs/export-template.md` | Initial (no changelog) |\n| `.vista/features/share-docs/specs/export-ui.md` | Initial (no changelog) |\n","numLines":818,"startLine":1,"totalLines":818}}}
