{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01NcE17LCvgZn3qyVJEPvGAn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good. Now I have a clear picture. For Phase 3 (Offline-First), the plan says to download and inline Tailwind CSS, Mermaid.js, and Marked.js. However, the approach of including massive vendor files (Tailwind's play CDN is a JS runtime, Mermaid is ~2MB, Marked is ~50KB) directly in the repo isn't great. Instead, I'll take a practical approach:\n\n1. For **Marked.js** (~50KB minified) — small enough to embed inline\n2. For **Mermaid.js** (~2MB minified) — too large for repo; we'll fetch at build time or use a reasonable bundled version\n3. For **Tailwind CSS** — instead of the CDN runtime, generate a pre-built CSS file with the specific utilities used\n\nThe pragmatic approach: when `offline=True`, we'll inline the CSS (as a pre-generated Tailwind output) and embed Marked.js and Mermaid.js into the HTML. Rather than storing massive vendor files, I'll create an `OfflineDepsService` that reads pre-downloaded files from a `vendor/` directory if they exist, and provides a mechanism to download them.\n\nLet me start implementing Phase 3 and Phase 4."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":336,"cache_read_input_tokens":78048,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":336},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6996de78-f515-44c4-bca3-90f28086b3f0","uuid":"f5e269f2-44fc-4771-81f4-d76d6f2c481b"}
